SUMMARY:Shimura varieties as moduli spaces for Hodge structures
DESCRIPTION:The usual definition of a Shimura variety is often unhelpful to
  beginners: one introduces a "Shimura datum" and defines complex manifolds
  as double quotients of adelic points of reductive groups. In this talk I 
 will attempt to motivate this definition by viewing Shimura varieties as m
 oduli spaces for Hodge structures.\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/1787
 4/
LOCATION:IHP
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17874/
